{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792577882156,"sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","part":{"partID":"prt_15df7c749001YlYtqvmejcNz78","sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","messageID":"msg_15df7bff6001X4rIK16ik9WE2m","type":"tool","id":"call_03_mZLGmZ3wMqzSQcCY4Gze0761","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/REVIEW_SCOPE.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/REVIEW_SCOPE.md, lines 1-214\n1: ## workflow\n2: \n3: ### 0\n4: \"Start the local server against a disposable data directory; initialize the SQLite schema on first\n5: start.\"\n6: \n7: ### 1\n8: \"Create the single home with POST /api/home, then add equipment records with POST /api/equipment\n9: anchored by home_id.\"\n10: \n11: ### 2\n12: \"Create care plans with POST /api/plans using interval_days and an optional equipment anchor.\"\n13: \n14: ### 3\n15: \"Query GET /api/tasks/due with an explicit as_of and horizon_days to see overdue, due, and upcoming\n16: work.\"\n17: \n18: ### 4\n19: \"Record a completion and note with POST /api/plans/{id}/completions; the same transaction updates\n20: the plan next due date.\"\n21: \n22: ### 5\n23: \"Read GET /api/plans/{id}/completions or GET /api/history filtered by home_id and equipment_id.\"\n24: \n25: ### 6\n26: \"Use GET / for the basic accessible single-page UI; all actions remain available through the\n27: documented JSON API.\"\n28: \n29: ## acceptance\n30: \n31: ### 0\n32: \"A fresh database has no home; POST /api/home creates exactly one record with id home, and a second\n33: POST returns 409 HOME_EXISTS without mutating the stored home.\"\n34: \n35: ### 1\n36: \"POST /api/equipment under the existing home returns 201 and round-trips through list and detail;\n37: blank names, invalid categories, and unknown homes return 422 or 404 and add no equipment row.\"\n38: \n39: ### 2\n40: \"POST /api/plans enforces interval_days 1..3650 and mutual exclusion of last_completed_on and\n41: first_due_on; GET /api/tasks/due returns exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at as_of and\n42: horizon_days boundaries, while invalid requests write nothing.\"\n43: \n44: ### 3\n45: \"A completion with note inserts one history row and atomically sets due_on to max(previous\n46: last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days; leap-day, month-end, year-end, future-date,\n47: oversize-note, and unknown-plan failures leave both plan and completions unchanged.\"\n48: \n49: ### 4\n50: \"GET /api/history filters by home and equipment and returns documented fields in descending\n51: completion order; invalid filters write nothing; GET / is dependency-free accessible HTML and\n52: unknown routes or methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n53: \n54: ## observations\n55: \n56: ### 0\n57: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 17, 17, \"Document claim: micasa describes itself as home maintenance\n58: from the terminal, a local tool rather than a hosted multi-tenant service.\"]\n59: \n60: ### 1\n61: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 25, 25, \"Document claim: the upstream advertises schedules, due\n62: dates, and full history.\"]\n63: \n64: ### 2\n65: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 104, 135, \"Code observation: HouseProfile stores\n66: address, year built, systems, and other attributes; no explicit multi-home ownership table is\n67: observed in the selected files.\"]\n68: \n69: ### 3\n70: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 201, 216, \"Code observation: Appliance stores make,\n71: model, serial, warranty, and location, with no home_id field observed.\"]\n72: \n73: ### 4\n74: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 218, 237, \"Code observation: MaintenanceItem has an\n75: optional ApplianceID, category, season, interval months, last serviced date, and due date.\"]\n76: \n77: ### 5\n78: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 261, 274, \"Code observation: ServiceLogEntry belongs\n79: to a maintenance item and stores serviced_at, optional vendor and cost, notes, and timestamps.\"]\n80: \n81: ### 6\n82: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_house.go\", 22, 31, \"Code observation: CreateHouseProfile\n83: counts existing profiles and rejects a second row, implementing one house profile.\"]\n84: \n85: ### 7\n86: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_maintenance.go\", 24, 33, \"Code observation:\n87: ListMaintenanceByAppliance filters maintenance items by appliance id, showing an equipment-anchored\n88: query path.\"]\n89: \n90: ### 8\n91: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\", 16, 30, \"Code observation:\n92: syncLastServiced sets LastServicedAt to the most recent non-deleted serviced_at.\"]\n93: \n94: ### 9\n95: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\", 59, 73, \"Code observation:\n96: CreateServiceLog runs in a transaction, creates the service log, then syncs the parent maintenance\n97: item.\"]\n98: \n99: ### 10\n100: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 168, 177, \"Code observation: ComputeNextDue\n101: returns an explicit due date when set, otherwise adds interval months to the last service date.\"]\n102: \n103: ### 11\n104: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 182, 192, \"Code observation: AddMonths clamps\n105: the day to the target month end, avoiding the Jan 31 plus one month overflow.\"]\n106: \n107: ### 12\n108: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 98, 153, \"Code observation: interval parsing\n109: accepts years and months, not days.\"]\n110: \n111: ### 13\n112: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/dashboard.go\", 12, 25, \"Code observation: scheduled maintenance\n113: is defined as interval months greater than zero or an explicit due date.\"]\n114: \n115: ### 14\n116: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 58, 58, \"Document claim: the upstream is pure Go using SQLite and a\n117: terminal UI; this target does not copy or run that implementation.\"]\n118: \n119: ## features\n120: \n121: ### 0\n122: \"Home and equipment anchor\"\n123: \n124: ### 1\n125: \"Every-N-day plan and due queue\"\n126: \n127: ### 2\n128: \"Completion and next-due rollover\"\n129: \n130: ### 3\n131: \"Anchored care history\"\n132: \n133: ### 4\n134: \"Accessible localhost UI\"\n135: \n136: ## goals\n137: \n138: ### 0\n139: \"In a dedicated data directory, create the single home, add an equipment record under it, and prove\n140: duplicate-home and invalid-equipment requests return 409, 422, or 404 without changing stored\n141: records.\"\n142: \n143: ### 1\n144: \"Create plans with interval_days in 1..3650 and verify GET /api/tasks/due returns the exact overdue,\n145: due, and upcoming sets at the as_of and horizon_days boundaries while invalid plans write nothing.\"\n146: \n147: ### 2\n148: \"Record a completion and note in one atomic call and verify due_on becomes max(previous\n149: last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days across leap-day, month-end, and year-end\n150: examples, with invalid completions leaving no trace.\"\n151: \n152: ### 3\n153: \"Retrieve completions filtered by home and equipment in documented descending order with plan and\n154: equipment names and notes, and reject invalid filters without writes.\"\n155: \n156: ### 4\n157: \"Load GET / and assert a dependency-free, labelled, keyboard-accessible HTML shell exposes home,\n158: equipment, plan, due, completion, and history workflows, while unknown routes and methods return\n159: documented JSON errors.\"\n160: \n161: ## gaps\n162: \n163: ### 0\n164: \"Upstream status: not_run. The repository was read as evidence only; no build, test, server, TUI, or\n165: database was executed, so no upstream behavior is runtime-verified.\"\n166: \n167: ### 1\n168: \"Runtime verification is not_run for the target too. The probe and architecture are authored\n169: artifacts; no server was started and no acceptance case was executed in this task.\"\n170: \n171: ### 2\n172: \"Single-home and single-user by design; no multi-property, accounts, authentication, sharing, or\n173: remote access.\"\n174: \n175: ### 3\n176: \"No notifications, email, SMS, push, calendar sync, or background scheduler; due work is pull-based\n177: through the API and UI.\"\n178: \n179: ### 4\n180: \"No costs, vendors, receipts, photos, manuals, warranties, projects, quotes, incidents, documents,\n181: or LLM features; those upstream surfaces are intentionally out of scope.\"\n182: \n183: ### 5\n184: \"Every-N-days recurrence differs from upstream interval months; no compatibility with upstream\n185: databases, APIs, or schema is claimed.\"\n186: \n187: ### 6\n188: \"No delete, undo, archive, or restore endpoints; completion history is append-only and test records\n189: remain until the disposable data directory is discarded.\"\n190: \n191: ### 7\n192: \"Validation is strict and date-only; natural-language dates and timezone conversion are unsupported.\n193: Server local date can differ by one day from a client in another timezone.\"\n194: \n195: ### 8\n196: \"The UI is a minimal single-page client, not a polished product; no internationalization, offline\n197: cache, or mobile-native behavior.\"\n198: \n199: ### 9\n200: \"Schema v1 has no migration path. Changing entities later needs an explicit migration or a new\n201: disposable database.\"\n202: \n203: ### 10\n204: \"Concurrency is sized for one user; SQLite WAL and busy_timeout reduce but do not eliminate lock\n205: contention.\"\n206: \n207: ### 11\n208: \"User decision points: confirm one-home scope, the default due date of creation day when no anchor\n209: is provided, latest-completion rollover for backdated entries, strict date-only input, and the\n210: absence of delete and defect-tracking features.\"\n211: \n212: ### 12\n213: \"Restart durability may be described as an operator stop and start step in README; it was not run\n214: and is not claimed as verified.\"","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/REVIEW_SCOPE.md, lines 1-214\n1: ## workflow\n2: \n3: ### 0\n4: \"Start the local server against a disposable data directory; initialize the SQLite schema on first\n5: start.\"\n6: \n7: ### 1\n8: \"Create the single home with POST /api/home, then add equipment records with POST /api/equipment\n9: anchored by home_id.\"\n10: \n11: ### 2\n12: \"Create care plans with POST /api/plans using interval_days and an optional equipment anchor.\"\n13: \n14: ### 3\n15: \"Query GET /api/tasks/due with an explicit as_of and horizon_days to see overdue, due, and upcoming\n16: work.\"\n17: \n18: ### 4\n19: \"Record a completion and note with POST /api/plans/{id}/completions; the same transaction updates\n20: the plan next due date.\"\n21: \n22: ### 5\n23: \"Read GET /api/plans/{id}/completions or GET /api/history filtered by home_id and equipment_id.\"\n24: \n25: ### 6\n26: \"Use GET / for the basic accessible single-page UI; all actions remain available through the\n27: documented JSON API.\"\n28: \n29: ## acceptance\n30: \n31: ### 0\n32: \"A fresh database has no home; POST /api/home creates exactly one record with id home, and a second\n33: POST returns 409 HOME_EXISTS without mutating the stored home.\"\n34: \n35: ### 1\n36: \"POST /api/equipment under the existing home returns 201 and round-trips through list and detail;\n37: blank names, invalid categories, and unknown homes return 422 or 404 and add no equipment row.\"\n38: \n39: ### 2\n40: \"POST /api/plans enforces interval_days 1..3650 and mutual exclusion of last_completed_on and\n41: first_due_on; GET /api/tasks/due returns exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at as_of and\n42: horizon_days boundaries, while invalid requests write nothing.\"\n43: \n44: ### 3\n45: \"A completion with note inserts one history row and atomically sets due_on to max(previous\n46: last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days; leap-day, month-end, year-end, future-date,\n47: oversize-note, and unknown-plan failures leave both plan and completions unchanged.\"\n48: \n49: ### 4\n50: \"GET /api/history filters by home and equipment and returns documented fields in descending\n51: completion order; invalid filters write nothing; GET / is dependency-free accessible HTML and\n52: unknown routes or methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n53: \n54: ## observations\n55: \n56: ### 0\n57: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 17, 17, \"Document claim: micasa describes itself as home maintenance\n58: from the terminal, a local tool rather than a hosted multi-tenant service.\"]\n59: \n60: ### 1\n61: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 25, 25, \"Document claim: the upstream advertises schedules, due\n62: dates, and full history.\"]\n63: \n64: ### 2\n65: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 104, 135, \"Code observation: HouseProfile stores\n66: address, year built, systems, and other attributes; no explicit multi-home ownership table is\n67: observed in the selected files.\"]\n68: \n69: ### 3\n70: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 201, 216, \"Code observation: Appliance stores make,\n71: model, serial, warranty, and location, with no home_id field observed.\"]\n72: \n73: ### 4\n74: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 218, 237, \"Code observation: MaintenanceItem has an\n75: optional ApplianceID, category, season, interval months, last serviced date, and due date.\"]\n76: \n77: ### 5\n78: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/models.go\", 261, 274, \"Code observation: ServiceLogEntry belongs\n79: to a maintenance item and stores serviced_at, optional vendor and cost, notes, and timestamps.\"]\n80: \n81: ### 6\n82: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_house.go\", 22, 31, \"Code observation: CreateHouseProfile\n83: counts existing profiles and rejects a second row, implementing one house profile.\"]\n84: \n85: ### 7\n86: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_maintenance.go\", 24, 33, \"Code observation:\n87: ListMaintenanceByAppliance filters maintenance items by appliance id, showing an equipment-anchored\n88: query path.\"]\n89: \n90: ### 8\n91: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\", 16, 30, \"Code observation:\n92: syncLastServiced sets LastServicedAt to the most recent non-deleted serviced_at.\"]\n93: \n94: ### 9\n95: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\", 59, 73, \"Code observation:\n96: CreateServiceLog runs in a transaction, creates the service log, then syncs the parent maintenance\n97: item.\"]\n98: \n99: ### 10\n100: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 168, 177, \"Code observation: ComputeNextDue\n101: returns an explicit due date when set, otherwise adds interval months to the last service date.\"]\n102: \n103: ### 11\n104: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 182, 192, \"Code observation: AddMonths clamps\n105: the day to the target month end, avoiding the Jan 31 plus one month overflow.\"]\n106: \n107: ### 12\n108: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/validation.go\", 98, 153, \"Code observation: interval parsing\n109: accepts years and months, not days.\"]\n110: \n111: ### 13\n112: [\"code_observation\", \"internal/data/dashboard.go\", 12, 25, \"Code observation: scheduled maintenance\n113: is defined as interval months greater than zero or an explicit due date.\"]\n114: \n115: ### 14\n116: [\"documentation\", \"README.md\", 58, 58, \"Document claim: the upstream is pure Go using SQLite and a\n117: terminal UI; this target does not copy or run that implementation.\"]\n118: \n119: ## features\n120: \n121: ### 0\n122: \"Home and equipment anchor\"\n123: \n124: ### 1\n125: \"Every-N-day plan and due queue\"\n126: \n127: ### 2\n128: \"Completion and next-due rollover\"\n129: \n130: ### 3\n131: \"Anchored care history\"\n132: \n133: ### 4\n134: \"Accessible localhost UI\"\n135: \n136: ## goals\n137: \n138: ### 0\n139: \"In a dedicated data directory, create the single home, add an equipment record under it, and prove\n140: duplicate-home and invalid-equipment requests return 409, 422, or 404 without changing stored\n141: records.\"\n142: \n143: ### 1\n144: \"Create plans with interval_days in 1..3650 and verify GET /api/tasks/due returns the exact overdue,\n145: due, and upcoming sets at the as_of and horizon_days boundaries while invalid plans write nothing.\"\n146: \n147: ### 2\n148: \"Record a completion and note in one atomic call and verify due_on becomes max(previous\n149: last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days across leap-day, month-end, and year-end\n150: examples, with invalid completions leaving no trace.\"\n151: \n152: ### 3\n153: \"Retrieve completions filtered by home and equipment in documented descending order with plan and\n154: equipment names and notes, and reject invalid filters without writes.\"\n155: \n156: ### 4\n157: \"Load GET / and assert a dependency-free, labelled, keyboard-accessible HTML shell exposes home,\n158: equipment, plan, due, completion, and history workflows, while unknown routes and methods return\n159: documented JSON errors.\"\n160: \n161: ## gaps\n162: \n163: ### 0\n164: \"Upstream status: not_run. The repository was read as evidence only; no build, test, server, TUI, or\n165: database was executed, so no upstream behavior is runtime-verified.\"\n166: \n167: ### 1\n168: \"Runtime verification is not_run for the target too. The probe and architecture are authored\n169: artifacts; no server was started and no acceptance case was executed in this task.\"\n170: \n171: ### 2\n172: \"Single-home and single-user by design; no multi-property, accounts, authentication, sharing, or\n173: remote access.\"\n174: \n175: ### 3\n176: \"No notifications, email, SMS, push, calendar sync, or background scheduler; due work is pull-based\n177: through the API and UI.\"\n178: \n179: ### 4\n180: \"No costs, vendors, receipts, photos, manuals, warranties, projects, quotes, incidents, documents,\n181: or LLM features; those upstream surfaces are intentionally out of scope.\"\n182: \n183: ### 5\n184: \"Every-N-days recurrence differs from upstream interval months; no compatibility with upstream\n185: databases, APIs, or schema is claimed.\"\n186: \n187: ### 6\n188: \"No delete, undo, archive, or restore endpoints; completion history is append-only and test records\n189: remain until the disposable data directory is discarded.\"\n190: \n191: ### 7\n192: \"Validation is strict and date-only; natural-language dates and timezone conversion are unsupported.\n193: Server local date can differ by one day from a client in another timezone.\"\n194: \n195: ### 8\n196: \"The UI is a minimal single-page client, not a polished product; no internationalization, offline\n197: cache, or mobile-native behavior.\"\n198: \n199: ### 9\n200: \"Schema v1 has no migration path. Changing entities later needs an explicit migration or a new\n201: disposable database.\"\n202: \n203: ### 10\n204: \"Concurrency is sized for one user; SQLite WAL and busy_timeout reduce but do not eliminate lock\n205: contention.\"\n206: \n207: ### 11\n208: \"User decision points: confirm one-home scope, the default due date of creation day when no anchor\n209: is provided, latest-completion rollover for backdated entries, strict date-only input, and the\n210: absence of delete and defect-tracking features.\"\n211: \n212: ### 12\n213: \"Restart durability may be described as an operator stop and start step in README; it was not run\n214: and is not claimed as verified.\""}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/REVIEW_SCOPE.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792577881929,"end":1792577882156}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1792577882241,"sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","part":{"id":"prt_15df7c881001z7MaAXmzvoe35j","sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","messageID":"msg_15df7bff6001X4rIK16ik9WE2m","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"ab4f6fa0e06592211cbe07afe6ea01155f2d9862","cost":0.0007889759999999999,"tokens":{"input":3816,"output":343,"reasoning":9,"cache":{"read":1792,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792577883924,"sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","part":{"id":"prt_15df7cf14001g5Ty2AmjKm21Dc","sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","messageID":"msg_15df7c8860016JL7lonLsh7LDU","type":"step-start","snapshot":"fdc4cd13e9ca88b09f98f2836e78a20de70ea9cb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792577884708,"sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","part":{"partID":"prt_15df7cfa9001xpMoXoq66JG24p","sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","messageID":"msg_15df7c8860016JL7lonLsh7LDU","type":"tool","id":"call_00_oAOwI0ij4fuum1OvNxjY9589","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/VIEW_ARCH.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/VIEW_ARCH.md, lines 1-168\n1: # Home Care Ledger: target architecture\n2: \n3: ## Scope and decisions to confirm\n4: - Local single-user target: one homeowner, one home, loopback only.\n5: - Python 3.11+ standard library only; SQLite; no third-party packages.\n6: - This is a cognition template, not an application and not the upstream micasa codebase.\n7: - Deliberately excluded: accounts and authentication, notifications, email, vendors, costs, quotes, projects, documents, manuals, photos, payments, LLM, multi-property, imports and exports, and deletion endpoints.\n8: - Decision: exactly one home with fixed id `home`, because the pinned scenario is the user's own home and upstream exposes a single house profile.\n9: - Decision: recurrence is every N calendar days, 1..3650, because the scenario says every N days. Upstream uses interval months; this target is not API-compatible with it.\n10: - Decision: a plan created without an anchor is due on the server local creation date.\n11: - Decision: a backdated completion never moves next due backwards; next due is based on the latest completion date.\n12: - Decision: no natural-language dates and no timezone-bearing timestamps in domain dates.\n13: \n14: ## Runtime, data directory, start\n15: - Source file `app.py`; database `$HOMECARE_DATA_DIR/homecare.sqlite3`.\n16: - `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR` defaults to `./data`; the directory is created if absent.\n17: - Start: `python3 app.py --data-dir ./data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765`.\n18: - Equivalent environment variables: `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR`, `HOMECARE_HOST`, `HOMECARE_PORT`.\n19: - Bind loopback by default. There is no authentication; do not expose the port.\n20: - On first start create schema and indexes. Schema version 1 is created once; no migration beyond that.\n21: - SQLite connection setup: `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`, `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000`.\n22: - Server: `ThreadingHTTPServer` is acceptable, but every write uses one explicit SQLite transaction.\n23: - JSON is UTF-8. Maximum request body 1,048,576 bytes. POST and PATCH must send `application/json`; otherwise 415.\n24: - Only GET, POST, and PATCH on documented routes. Other methods return 405 `METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED`.\n25: - Health: `GET /health` returns `{status: ok, database: ready}`.\n26: \n27: ## Entities and exact persisted fields\n28: `homes`\n29: - `id` TEXT primary key, always the literal `home`.\n30: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80 Unicode code points.\n31: - `address` TEXT NOT NULL default empty string, trimmed, 0..200.\n32: - `created_at`, `updated_at` TEXT UTC ISO-8601 with `Z`, for example `2026-10-21T08:30:00Z`.\n33: \n34: `equipment`\n35: - `id` TEXT primary key, `eq_` plus 32 lowercase hex characters.\n36: - `home_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES `homes(id)` ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n37: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80.\n38: - `category` TEXT NOT NULL, one of `heating`, `cooling`, `plumbing`, `electrical`, `roof`, `exterior`, `appliance`, `safety`, `other`.\n39: - `location` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n40: - `make` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n41: - `model` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n42: - `installed_on` TEXT NULL, strict calendar date 1900-01-01..2100-12-31.\n43: - `created_at`, `updated_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n44: \n45: `plans`\n46: - `id` TEXT primary key, `pl_` plus 32 hex.\n47: - `home_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES homes.\n48: - `equipment_id` TEXT NULL REFERENCES equipment; when present it must belong to the same `home_id`.\n49: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80.\n50: - `interval_days` INTEGER NOT NULL, 1..3650 inclusive.\n51: - `last_completed_on` TEXT NULL, strict date; latest known care date.\n52: - `due_on` TEXT NOT NULL, strict date.\n53: - `notes` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..500.\n54: - `created_at`, `updated_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n55: - Index: `(home_id, equipment_id, due_on)`.\n56: \n57: `completions`\n58: - `id` TEXT primary key, `cm_` plus 32 hex.\n59: - `plan_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES plans ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n60: - `completed_on` TEXT NOT NULL, strict date.\n61: - `note` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, trimmed, 0..500.\n62: - `created_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n63: - Index: `(plan_id, completed_on DESC, created_at DESC)`.\n64: - There is no PATCH or DELETE for completions: the record is append-only.\n65: \n66: ## Date, validation and recurrence rules\n67: - Domain dates are `YYYY-MM-DD` only. Reject timestamps, natural language, invalid ordinal dates, and years outside 1900..2100 with 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`.\n68: - `server_today` is `datetime.date.today()` in the host local timezone. Domain dates are not converted between zones.\n69: - Creation response timestamps are UTC; domain decisions use `server_today` or an explicit `as_of`.\n70: - Plan anchor when created:\n71:   - `first_due_on` supplied: `due_on = first_due_on`.\n72:   - else `last_completed_on` supplied: `due_on = last_completed_on + interval_days`.\n73:   - else: `due_on = server_today`.\n74: - `last_completed_on` and `first_due_on` are mutually exclusive; supplying both is 422.\n75: - `last_completed_on` may not be after `server_today`; `first_due_on` may not be before 1900-01-01 or after 2100-12-31.\n76: - Completion accepts `completed_on <= server_today`.\n77: - Next due after a completion is always `max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) + interval_days`, using proleptic Gregorian ordinal addition. This makes backdated entries safe and never regresses the schedule.\n78: - If a plan was seeded with `last_completed_on`, that seed is not a completion record; only completion rows appear in history.\n79: - Due status at `as_of`: `overdue` when `due_on < as_of`; `due` when equal; `upcoming` when greater.\n80: - Due query includes tasks with `due_on <= as_of + horizon_days`. Default `horizon_days=0`, so default shows overdue and due only. Horizon range 0..365.\n81: - Sort order: due tasks by `due_on ASC, created_at ASC, id ASC`; plans by `created_at ASC, id ASC`; completions and history by `completed_on DESC, created_at DESC, id DESC`.\n82: - Date edge examples: 2024-02-28 + 1 = 2024-02-29; 2024-02-29 + 1 = 2024-03-01; 2024-12-31 + 30 = 2025-01-30; 2026-01-31 + 31 = 2026-03-03.\n83: - Integer fields reject booleans, floats, and numeric strings; JSON boolean true is not an integer. Query integers use decimal digits only.\n84: \n85: ## HTTP API\n86: Base URL in examples: `http://127.0.0.1:8765`.\n87: \n88: Common response rules:\n89: - All API responses are JSON objects with `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n90: - Error shape: `error` object with `code` string, `message` string, and `field` string or null.\n91: - Codes and statuses:\n92:   - `INVALID_JSON` 400\n93:   - `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` 415\n94:   - `METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED` 405\n95:   - `NOT_FOUND` 404 for an unknown route\n96:   - `HOME_NOT_FOUND` 404\n97:   - `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` 404\n98:   - `PLAN_NOT_FOUND` 404\n99:   - `HOME_EXISTS` 409\n100:   - `VALIDATION_ERROR` 422\n101:   - `INTERNAL_ERROR` 500 with no leaked internals\n102: - Unknown request fields are rejected with 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` and `field` naming the first unknown field.\n103: - Canonical plan object: `id`, `home_id`, `equipment_id`, `name`, `interval_days`, `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, `notes`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `completion_count`, and `status`. `status` is computed against `server_today`.\n104: - Canonical completion object: `id`, `plan_id`, `completed_on`, `note`, and `created_at`.\n105: \n106: ### Home\n107: `POST /api/home`\n108: Body: `name` required, `address` optional. Returns 201 `{home: HOME}`. If a home already exists returns 409 `HOME_EXISTS` and writes nothing.\n109: `GET /api/home` returns 200 `{home: HOME}` or 404 `HOME_NOT_FOUND`.\n110: `PATCH /api/home` Body: at least one of `name`, `address`; validates bounds. Returns 200 `{home: HOME}`. Empty patch 422. There is no DELETE.\n111: \n112: ### Equipment\n113: `POST /api/equipment`\n114: Body: `home_id` required, `name` required, `category` required, optional `location`, `make`, `model`, and `installed_on`.\n115: Returns 201 `{equipment: EQUIPMENT}`. Unknown home 404 `HOME_NOT_FOUND`.\n116: `GET /api/equipment?home_id=home` returns 200 `{equipment: [EQUIPMENT...]}` sorted by `created_at ASC, id ASC`. Missing `home_id` 422; unknown home 404.\n117: `GET /api/equipment/{id}` returns 200 `{equipment: EQUIPMENT}` or 404 `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`.\n118: No delete.\n119: \n120: ### Plans\n121: `POST /api/plans`\n122: Body: `home_id` required; `name` required; `interval_days` required; optional `equipment_id`, `last_completed_on`, `first_due_on`, and `notes`.\n123: Returns 201 `{plan: PLAN}`. Unknown home 404. Unknown equipment 404 `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`; equipment belonging to another home 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` with field `equipment_id` (defensive, unreachable while only one home exists).\n124: `GET /api/plans?home_id=home&equipment_id=eq_...` returns 200 `{plans: [PLAN...]}`. `equipment_id` is an optional filter. Missing home 422; unknown home 404; unknown equipment 404.\n125: `GET /api/plans/{id}` returns 200 `{plan: PLAN}` or 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`.\n126: No interval or schedule edit endpoint in this version; create a new plan instead. This is a deliberate scope cut.\n127: \n128: ### Due work\n129: `GET /api/tasks/due?home_id=home&as_of=YYYY-MM-DD&horizon_days=0&equipment_id=eq_...`\n130: - `home_id` required; `as_of` optional, default `server_today`; `horizon_days` optional integer 0..365; `equipment_id` optional.\n131: - Returns 200 `{as_of, horizon_days, tasks: [TASK...]}`.\n132: - TASK fields: `id` (plan id), `home_id`, `home_name`, `equipment_id`, `equipment_name` or null, `name`, `interval_days`, `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, `status`, `days_until_due`, and `notes`.\n133: - `days_until_due = due_on - as_of` in days; negative means overdue.\n134: - Invalid `as_of`, out-of-range horizon, missing home, or unknown home or equipment: 422 or 404 as applicable. No writes.\n135: \n136: ### Completions and history\n137: `POST /api/plans/{id}/completions`\n138: Body: `completed_on` required, `note` optional default empty.\n139: Returns 201 `{completion: COMPLETION, plan: PLAN}`. Unknown plan 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`. Future date, bad date, or note over 500: 422. The insert and plan update happen in one transaction; on any failure neither changes.\n140: `GET /api/plans/{id}/completions` returns 200 `{completions: [COMPLETION...]}` or 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`.\n141: `GET /api/history?home_id=home&equipment_id=eq_...&limit=100`\n142: - `home_id` required; `equipment_id` optional; `limit` 1..500 default 100.\n143: - Returns 200 `{history: [HISTORY...]}` sorted as defined above.\n144: - HISTORY fields: `id`, `plan_id`, `plan_name`, `home_id`, `home_name`, `equipment_id`, `equipment_name` or null, `completed_on`, `note`, and `created_at`.\n145: - Missing home 422; unknown home or equipment 404. No writes.\n146: \n147: ## Atomic failure semantics\n148: - Validate method, content type, JSON, field presence, types, bounds, enums, dates, and referential checks before opening a write transaction.\n149: - For `POST /api/home`, insert with fixed id `home`; a concurrent duplicate loses with 409 and leaves exactly one row.\n150: - For `POST /api/equipment` and `POST /api/plans`, one INSERT each; foreign-key failure maps to 404 or 422, not 500.\n151: - For completion, `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`; select plan; compute `last = max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on)`; INSERT completion; UPDATE plan `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, and `updated_at`; COMMIT. Any error triggers ROLLBACK, leaving zero new completions and an unchanged plan.\n152: - Reads never create rows. A failed request must produce no completion, no plan, no equipment, and no home mutation.\n153: - SQLite constraint errors are mapped to a deterministic 422 or 409; unexpected errors return 500 `INTERNAL_ERROR` without partial commits.\n154: \n155: ## Basic accessible UI\n156: `GET /` returns one HTML document with `lang=en`, UTF-8, no external assets, and a small inline script that calls the JSON API.\n157: - Sections, in order: Home; Equipment; Care plans; Due work; Completion history.\n158: - Every input has a visible `label for` tied to an id; groups use `fieldset` and `legend`.\n159: - Buttons are native `button` elements with descriptive text: Create home, Add equipment, Add plan, Record completion, Refresh.\n160: - Due table has `caption`, `th scope=col`, and text status plus a non-color-only overdue label.\n161: - Success and validation messages render in a container with `role=status` and `aria-live=polite`; errors also include the field name.\n162: - Forms are keyboard operable, visible focus is retained, default browser font sizing is not disabled, and no timeout or auto-submit is used.\n163: - Completing a task opens a small form for `completed_on` and `note`; the API response updates the due list and history without a full page reload.\n164: - History has home and equipment filters populated from the API.\n165: - The UI is a convenience surface; all behavior is available through the documented API.\n166: \n167: ## Probe contract\n168: `probe.py` is a standard-library HTTP client supplied in `acceptance_files`. It accepts `--base-url` and exactly one `--case A01..A05`, creates only disposable records with a unique suffix, never deletes, and asserts exact statuses, shapes, dates, ordering, and zero-write outcomes. It does not start the server and makes no claim about an upstream run.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/VIEW_ARCH.md, lines 1-168\n1: # Home Care Ledger: target architecture\n2: \n3: ## Scope and decisions to confirm\n4: - Local single-user target: one homeowner, one home, loopback only.\n5: - Python 3.11+ standard library only; SQLite; no third-party packages.\n6: - This is a cognition template, not an application and not the upstream micasa codebase.\n7: - Deliberately excluded: accounts and authentication, notifications, email, vendors, costs, quotes, projects, documents, manuals, photos, payments, LLM, multi-property, imports and exports, and deletion endpoints.\n8: - Decision: exactly one home with fixed id `home`, because the pinned scenario is the user's own home and upstream exposes a single house profile.\n9: - Decision: recurrence is every N calendar days, 1..3650, because the scenario says every N days. Upstream uses interval months; this target is not API-compatible with it.\n10: - Decision: a plan created without an anchor is due on the server local creation date.\n11: - Decision: a backdated completion never moves next due backwards; next due is based on the latest completion date.\n12: - Decision: no natural-language dates and no timezone-bearing timestamps in domain dates.\n13: \n14: ## Runtime, data directory, start\n15: - Source file `app.py`; database `$HOMECARE_DATA_DIR/homecare.sqlite3`.\n16: - `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR` defaults to `./data`; the directory is created if absent.\n17: - Start: `python3 app.py --data-dir ./data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765`.\n18: - Equivalent environment variables: `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR`, `HOMECARE_HOST`, `HOMECARE_PORT`.\n19: - Bind loopback by default. There is no authentication; do not expose the port.\n20: - On first start create schema and indexes. Schema version 1 is created once; no migration beyond that.\n21: - SQLite connection setup: `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`, `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000`.\n22: - Server: `ThreadingHTTPServer` is acceptable, but every write uses one explicit SQLite transaction.\n23: - JSON is UTF-8. Maximum request body 1,048,576 bytes. POST and PATCH must send `application/json`; otherwise 415.\n24: - Only GET, POST, and PATCH on documented routes. Other methods return 405 `METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED`.\n25: - Health: `GET /health` returns `{status: ok, database: ready}`.\n26: \n27: ## Entities and exact persisted fields\n28: `homes`\n29: - `id` TEXT primary key, always the literal `home`.\n30: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80 Unicode code points.\n31: - `address` TEXT NOT NULL default empty string, trimmed, 0..200.\n32: - `created_at`, `updated_at` TEXT UTC ISO-8601 with `Z`, for example `2026-10-21T08:30:00Z`.\n33: \n34: `equipment`\n35: - `id` TEXT primary key, `eq_` plus 32 lowercase hex characters.\n36: - `home_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES `homes(id)` ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n37: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80.\n38: - `category` TEXT NOT NULL, one of `heating`, `cooling`, `plumbing`, `electrical`, `roof`, `exterior`, `appliance`, `safety`, `other`.\n39: - `location` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n40: - `make` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n41: - `model` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..80.\n42: - `installed_on` TEXT NULL, strict calendar date 1900-01-01..2100-12-31.\n43: - `created_at`, `updated_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n44: \n45: `plans`\n46: - `id` TEXT primary key, `pl_` plus 32 hex.\n47: - `home_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES homes.\n48: - `equipment_id` TEXT NULL REFERENCES equipment; when present it must belong to the same `home_id`.\n49: - `name` TEXT NOT NULL, trimmed, 1..80.\n50: - `interval_days` INTEGER NOT NULL, 1..3650 inclusive.\n51: - `last_completed_on` TEXT NULL, strict date; latest known care date.\n52: - `due_on` TEXT NOT NULL, strict date.\n53: - `notes` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, 0..500.\n54: - `created_at`, `updated_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n55: - Index: `(home_id, equipment_id, due_on)`.\n56: \n57: `completions`\n58: - `id` TEXT primary key, `cm_` plus 32 hex.\n59: - `plan_id` TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES plans ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n60: - `completed_on` TEXT NOT NULL, strict date.\n61: - `note` TEXT NOT NULL default empty, trimmed, 0..500.\n62: - `created_at` UTC ISO-8601.\n63: - Index: `(plan_id, completed_on DESC, created_at DESC)`.\n64: - There is no PATCH or DELETE for completions: the record is append-only.\n65: \n66: ## Date, validation and recurrence rules\n67: - Domain dates are `YYYY-MM-DD` only. Reject timestamps, natural language, invalid ordinal dates, and years outside 1900..2100 with 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`.\n68: - `server_today` is `datetime.date.today()` in the host local timezone. Domain dates are not converted between zones.\n69: - Creation response timestamps are UTC; domain decisions use `server_today` or an explicit `as_of`.\n70: - Plan anchor when created:\n71:   - `first_due_on` supplied: `due_on = first_due_on`.\n72:   - else `last_completed_on` supplied: `due_on = last_completed_on + interval_days`.\n73:   - else: `due_on = server_today`.\n74: - `last_completed_on` and `first_due_on` are mutually exclusive; supplying both is 422.\n75: - `last_completed_on` may not be after `server_today`; `first_due_on` may not be before 1900-01-01 or after 2100-12-31.\n76: - Completion accepts `completed_on <= server_today`.\n77: - Next due after a completion is always `max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) + interval_days`, using proleptic Gregorian ordinal addition. This makes backdated entries safe and never regresses the schedule.\n78: - If a plan was seeded with `last_completed_on`, that seed is not a completion record; only completion rows appear in history.\n79: - Due status at `as_of`: `overdue` when `due_on < as_of`; `due` when equal; `upcoming` when greater.\n80: - Due query includes tasks with `due_on <= as_of + horizon_days`. Default `horizon_days=0`, so default shows overdue and due only. Horizon range 0..365.\n81: - Sort order: due tasks by `due_on ASC, created_at ASC, id ASC`; plans by `created_at ASC, id ASC`; completions and history by `completed_on DESC, created_at DESC, id DESC`.\n82: - Date edge examples: 2024-02-28 + 1 = 2024-02-29; 2024-02-29 + 1 = 2024-03-01; 2024-12-31 + 30 = 2025-01-30; 2026-01-31 + 31 = 2026-03-03.\n83: - Integer fields reject booleans, floats, and numeric strings; JSON boolean true is not an integer. Query integers use decimal digits only.\n84: \n85: ## HTTP API\n86: Base URL in examples: `http://127.0.0.1:8765`.\n87: \n88: Common response rules:\n89: - All API responses are JSON objects with `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n90: - Error shape: `error` object with `code` string, `message` string, and `field` string or null.\n91: - Codes and statuses:\n92:   - `INVALID_JSON` 400\n93:   - `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` 415\n94:   - `METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED` 405\n95:   - `NOT_FOUND` 404 for an unknown route\n96:   - `HOME_NOT_FOUND` 404\n97:   - `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` 404\n98:   - `PLAN_NOT_FOUND` 404\n99:   - `HOME_EXISTS` 409\n100:   - `VALIDATION_ERROR` 422\n101:   - `INTERNAL_ERROR` 500 with no leaked internals\n102: - Unknown request fields are rejected with 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` and `field` naming the first unknown field.\n103: - Canonical plan object: `id`, `home_id`, `equipment_id`, `name`, `interval_days`, `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, `notes`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `completion_count`, and `status`. `status` is computed against `server_today`.\n104: - Canonical completion object: `id`, `plan_id`, `completed_on`, `note`, and `created_at`.\n105: \n106: ### Home\n107: `POST /api/home`\n108: Body: `name` required, `address` optional. Returns 201 `{home: HOME}`. If a home already exists returns 409 `HOME_EXISTS` and writes nothing.\n109: `GET /api/home` returns 200 `{home: HOME}` or 404 `HOME_NOT_FOUND`.\n110: `PATCH /api/home` Body: at least one of `name`, `address`; validates bounds. Returns 200 `{home: HOME}`. Empty patch 422. There is no DELETE.\n111: \n112: ### Equipment\n113: `POST /api/equipment`\n114: Body: `home_id` required, `name` required, `category` required, optional `location`, `make`, `model`, and `installed_on`.\n115: Returns 201 `{equipment: EQUIPMENT}`. Unknown home 404 `HOME_NOT_FOUND`.\n116: `GET /api/equipment?home_id=home` returns 200 `{equipment: [EQUIPMENT...]}` sorted by `created_at ASC, id ASC`. Missing `home_id` 422; unknown home 404.\n117: `GET /api/equipment/{id}` returns 200 `{equipment: EQUIPMENT}` or 404 `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`.\n118: No delete.\n119: \n120: ### Plans\n121: `POST /api/plans`\n122: Body: `home_id` required; `name` required; `interval_days` required; optional `equipment_id`, `last_completed_on`, `first_due_on`, and `notes`.\n123: Returns 201 `{plan: PLAN}`. Unknown home 404. Unknown equipment 404 `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`; equipment belonging to another home 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` with field `equipment_id` (defensive, unreachable while only one home exists).\n124: `GET /api/plans?home_id=home&equipment_id=eq_...` returns 200 `{plans: [PLAN...]}`. `equipment_id` is an optional filter. Missing home 422; unknown home 404; unknown equipment 404.\n125: `GET /api/plans/{id}` returns 200 `{plan: PLAN}` or 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`.\n126: No interval or schedule edit endpoint in this version; create a new plan instead. This is a deliberate scope cut.\n127: \n128: ### Due work\n129: `GET /api/tasks/due?home_id=home&as_of=YYYY-MM-DD&horizon_days=0&equipment_id=eq_...`\n130: - `home_id` required; `as_of` optional, default `server_today`; `horizon_days` optional integer 0..365; `equipment_id` optional.\n131: - Returns 200 `{as_of, horizon_days, tasks: [TASK...]}`.\n132: - TASK fields: `id` (plan id), `home_id`, `home_name`, `equipment_id`, `equipment_name` or null, `name`, `interval_days`, `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, `status`, `days_until_due`, and `notes`.\n133: - `days_until_due = due_on - as_of` in days; negative means overdue.\n134: - Invalid `as_of`, out-of-range horizon, missing home, or unknown home or equipment: 422 or 404 as applicable. No writes.\n135: \n136: ### Completions and history\n137: `POST /api/plans/{id}/completions`\n138: Body: `completed_on` required, `note` optional default empty.\n139: Returns 201 `{completion: COMPLETION, plan: PLAN}`. Unknown plan 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`. Future date, bad date, or note over 500: 422. The insert and plan update happen in one transaction; on any failure neither changes.\n140: `GET /api/plans/{id}/completions` returns 200 `{completions: [COMPLETION...]}` or 404 `PLAN_NOT_FOUND`.\n141: `GET /api/history?home_id=home&equipment_id=eq_...&limit=100`\n142: - `home_id` required; `equipment_id` optional; `limit` 1..500 default 100.\n143: - Returns 200 `{history: [HISTORY...]}` sorted as defined above.\n144: - HISTORY fields: `id`, `plan_id`, `plan_name`, `home_id`, `home_name`, `equipment_id`, `equipment_name` or null, `completed_on`, `note`, and `created_at`.\n145: - Missing home 422; unknown home or equipment 404. No writes.\n146: \n147: ## Atomic failure semantics\n148: - Validate method, content type, JSON, field presence, types, bounds, enums, dates, and referential checks before opening a write transaction.\n149: - For `POST /api/home`, insert with fixed id `home`; a concurrent duplicate loses with 409 and leaves exactly one row.\n150: - For `POST /api/equipment` and `POST /api/plans`, one INSERT each; foreign-key failure maps to 404 or 422, not 500.\n151: - For completion, `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`; select plan; compute `last = max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on)`; INSERT completion; UPDATE plan `last_completed_on`, `due_on`, and `updated_at`; COMMIT. Any error triggers ROLLBACK, leaving zero new completions and an unchanged plan.\n152: - Reads never create rows. A failed request must produce no completion, no plan, no equipment, and no home mutation.\n153: - SQLite constraint errors are mapped to a deterministic 422 or 409; unexpected errors return 500 `INTERNAL_ERROR` without partial commits.\n154: \n155: ## Basic accessible UI\n156: `GET /` returns one HTML document with `lang=en`, UTF-8, no external assets, and a small inline script that calls the JSON API.\n157: - Sections, in order: Home; Equipment; Care plans; Due work; Completion history.\n158: - Every input has a visible `label for` tied to an id; groups use `fieldset` and `legend`.\n159: - Buttons are native `button` elements with descriptive text: Create home, Add equipment, Add plan, Record completion, Refresh.\n160: - Due table has `caption`, `th scope=col`, and text status plus a non-color-only overdue label.\n161: - Success and validation messages render in a container with `role=status` and `aria-live=polite`; errors also include the field name.\n162: - Forms are keyboard operable, visible focus is retained, default browser font sizing is not disabled, and no timeout or auto-submit is used.\n163: - Completing a task opens a small form for `completed_on` and `note`; the API response updates the due list and history without a full page reload.\n164: - History has home and equipment filters populated from the API.\n165: - The UI is a convenience surface; all behavior is available through the documented API.\n166: \n167: ## Probe contract\n168: `probe.py` is a standard-library HTTP client supplied in `acceptance_files`. It accepts `--base-url` and exactly one `--case A01..A05`, creates only disposable records with a unique suffix, never deletes, and asserts exact statuses, shapes, dates, ordering, and zero-write outcomes. It does not start the server and makes no claim about an upstream run."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/VIEW_ARCH.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792577884074,"end":1792577884708}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792577884709,"sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","part":{"partID":"prt_15df7d079001GmGGYWF8Ze7g0y","sessionID":"ses_ea208589fffeY8gRHkM8pRFG1I","messageID":"msg_15df7c8860016JL7lonLsh7LDU","type":"tool","id":"call_01_vt2arhwcoYHvkYCGBYci3509","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md, lines 1-36\n1: # Home Care Ledger acceptance probe\n2: \n3: This probe is a standard-library HTTP client for the target described in the blueprint. It creates records with a unique suffix, never deletes, and is intended for a disposable data directory.\n4: \n5: ## Prerequisites\n6: - Python 3.11 or newer.\n7: - The target server running locally.\n8: - A fresh disposable data directory. Do not point it at real household data.\n9: \n10: ## Start the target\n11: ```sh\n12: HOMECARE_DATA_DIR=./probe-data python3 app.py --data-dir ./probe-data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765\n13: ```\n14: The server stores `homecare.sqlite3` in the data directory and binds loopback only. There is no authentication.\n15: \n16: ## Run one case\n17: ```sh\n18: python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case A01\n19: ```\n20: Cases:\n21: - A01 home and equipment anchor, duplicate and invalid zero-write checks.\n22: - A02 plan bounds, due statuses, and as_of and horizon edges.\n23: - A03 completion, note, leap and month and year date edges, rollback checks.\n24: - A04 home and equipment history ordering and filters.\n25: - A05 accessible HTML shell, unknown route, and method errors.\n26: \n27: Run cases one at a time or all five sequentially against the same disposable database. Each case creates unique records.\n28: \n29: ## Expected result\n30: The script prints `PASS A0N` and exits 0 when every assertion passes. It prints `FAIL A0N: ...` or `ERROR A0N: ...` and exits 1 otherwise. A failure is evidence of a contract mismatch, not a reason to weaken the documented contract.\n31: \n32: ## Restart\n33: Operator stop and start can be tested manually by stopping the server, starting it again with the same `--data-dir`, and re-reading the records. This is an operator step and was not automated here.\n34: \n35: ## Runtime status\n36: not_run. The target and probe were authored, not executed. No upstream build or run was performed. No certification is claimed.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md, lines 1-36\n1: # Home Care Ledger acceptance probe\n2: \n3: This probe is a standard-library HTTP client for the target described in the blueprint. It creates records with a unique suffix, never deletes, and is intended for a disposable data directory.\n4: \n5: ## Prerequisites\n6: - Python 3.11 or newer.\n7: - The target server running locally.\n8: - A fresh disposable data directory. Do not point it at real household data.\n9: \n10: ## Start the target\n11: ```sh\n12: HOMECARE_DATA_DIR=./probe-data python3 app.py --data-dir ./probe-data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765\n13: ```\n14: The server stores `homecare.sqlite3` in the data directory and binds loopback only. There is no authentication.\n15: \n16: ## Run one case\n17: ```sh\n18: python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case A01\n19: ```\n20: Cases:\n21: - A01 home and equipment anchor, duplicate and invalid zero-write checks.\n22: - A02 plan bounds, due statuses, and as_of and horizon edges.\n23: - A03 completion, note, leap and month and year date edges, rollback checks.\n24: - A04 home and equipment history ordering and filters.\n25: - A05 accessible HTML shell, unknown route, and method errors.\n26: \n27: Run cases one at a time or all five sequentially against the same disposable database. Each case creates unique records.\n28: \n29: ## Expected result\n30: The script prints `PASS A0N` and exits 0 when every assertion passes. It prints `FAIL A0N: ...` or `ERROR A0N: ...` and exits 1 otherwise. A failure is evidence of a contract mismatch, not a reason to weaken the documented contract.\n31: \n32: ## Restart\n33: Operator stop and start can be tested manually by stopping the server, starting it again with the same `--data-dir`, and re-reading the records. This is an operator step and was not automated here.\n34: \n35: ## Runtime status\n36: not_run. The target and probe were authored, not executed. No upstream build or run was performed. No certification is claimed."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-home-care-revision-2026-10-21/home-care-r1/calls/blueprint-generate-aux-revision-1/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792577884281,"end":1792577884709}}}}
